^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
dropped the body
--
N5008 [temp.deduct.call]/1, [temp.variadic]/5: in libc++'s __has_construct
partial specialization, `declval<A>().construct(declval<Args>()...)' calls
`template <class U, class... Args> construct(U *, Args &&...)' with the
arguments storage *, path, path, so U = storage and the member template's
pack is {path, path}. The front end deduces the pack as EMPTY and
instantiates `construct<storage>()' ("instantiating
'alloc<storage>::construct' with <struct storage>"), whose body `::new(p)
U()' is ill-formed (storage has no default constructor) and is reported
dropped. The trait's value and the real call are right; the spurious drop
hides real drops. A direct call with explicit U and deduced pack works, so
the trigger is the pack of declval call arguments in a decltype of a
partial specialization. libc++'s
allocator<filesystem_error::_Storage>::construct (allocator.h:172),
reached from make_shared<_Storage>(path, path) in <filesystem>:
cpp17_filesystem_basic_libcxx and cpp17_filesystem_path_ops_libcxx
(round-163 audit). Header-free. Fixed in round 163i: a call argument over
a type pack is expanded outside function bodies too
(test_pattern_pack.desc, test_type_pack_arguments.desc). Fails on bin53.
